<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of Bologna</h1><p class="st-meta">1116 CE – 1506 CE (approx.) · capital Bologna</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The city-republic of Europe's oldest university and its forest of towers, which held a captive king for 23 years and later flourished under the Bentivoglio.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1116 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-v-holy-roman-emperor">Emperor Henry V</a> granted privileges to the citizens of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bologna">Bologna</a>, the starting point of the commune. Its law school, traditionally dated to 1088 and associated with the jurist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/irnerius">Irnerius</a>, drew students from all over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> and made the city famous.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bologna">Bologna</a> was ruled by consuls, then a podestà and popular councils. Noble families built hundreds of defensive towers, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/two-towers-bologna">Asinelli</a> and Garisenda. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guelphs-and-ghibellines">Guelph</a> Bologna captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enzo-of-sardinia">King Enzo</a>, son of Frederick II, at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-fossalta">Fossalta</a> in 1249 and held him until his death in 1272; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liber-paradisus">Liber Paradisus</a> of 1256 freed the serfs of its countryside. Nominally under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/papal-states">Papal States</a>, the city was dominated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepoli-family">Pepoli</a> and then the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bentivoglio-family">Bentivoglio</a> families.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-julius-ii">Pope Julius II</a> marched on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bologna">Bologna</a> in 1506 and drove out <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giovanni-ii-bentivoglio">Giovanni II Bentivoglio</a>. The city then passed under direct papal rule, which lasted until 1796, when it briefly became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bolognese-republic">Bolognese Republic</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 1116 CE – 1506 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:81.91%;width:7.76%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1116 CE – 1506 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bologna</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Taddeo Pepoli, Sante Bentivoglio, Giovanni II Bentivoglio</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Emilian, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Commune of Bologna, Bentivoglio Bologna, Bologna</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1311&amp;focus=republic-of-bologna" aria-label="Republic of Bologna on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4951 604 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Republic of Bologna lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5271 860L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5271 860h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5271 860h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Bologna. <a href="/atlas?year=1311&amp;focus=republic-of-bologna">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

